From 545ce3953b03f09ee7ceb3caee670e01a81421c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:43:10 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] feat(phase2): auto-edit harness, CUDA-less
 transcription fallback, loudness + boundary QC (WIP)

Phase 2 work in progress, committed at a safe checkpoint.
- media/transcription.py: missing CUDA libraries (cuBLAS/cuDNN) on a GPU
  host now fall back to CPU int8 once and are remembered for the process
  (previously: crash, then a hang in the batched retry ladder).
  WHISPER_DEVICE=cpu|cuda override.
- media/clip_qc.py: opt-in warn-only checks: loudness vs a LUFS target,
  complete-thought boundaries (opens/ends mid-sentence, cuts a word).
  Skipped when inputs are absent, so existing reports are unchanged.
- tools/phase2/auto_edit.py + run_all.py: drive the real stages per niche
  (transcribe, AI select or fixed windows, build_edl, attach_reframe_plan,
  stock resolve with keys, create_optimized_clip, QC, report).
Tests: test_broll_v3_cadence 28 (incl. 2 CUDA cases), test_clip_qc_phase2 5,
test_clip_qc_pipeline 8, test_separation_transcription 8 pass.
test_clip_qc and test_faster_whisper_transcription time out on Windows on
the untouched baseline too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
